 \"Prompt recall of concepts required for this lesson. Keep it brief and diagnostic.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Surface prerequisite knowledge\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Require selection and use of the learned idea in a recognizable context.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"apply\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Use knowledge in a familiar situation\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The teacher needs to know right now whether the objective landed, and correct-versus-incorrect is the signal being read.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"check-understanding\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'wrong answers must identify WHICH wrong model the learner holds\\', \\'practise-independent\\': \\'the purpose is rehearsal rather than measurement\\', \\'reflect\\': \\'there is no correct answer\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Detect immediate misunderstanding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Provide or elicit a rule for category membership and contrast borderline cases.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"classify\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Organize examples into categories\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Two or more named things must be told apart, and the same criteria apply to each.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"compare\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'classify\\': \\'instances are being sorted by a rule rather than two things contrasted\\', \\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'one side is a wrong belief, not a legitimate alternative\\', \\'evaluate\\': \\'one option must be judged better, not merely distinguished\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Expose similarities and differences\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Show which prior idea is being reused and exactly how it supports the current task.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"connect-back\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Make prerequisite dependence explicit\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State what the current idea enables next and the unresolved question that follows.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"connect-forward\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Bridge current learning to the next idea\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Give a precise learner-appropriate definition, distinguish it from nearby terms, and include notation only when useful.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"define\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Establish precise meaning\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner has not yet seen the method carried out end to end on a real instance, and the method is unambiguous once seen. If the learner has already seen it worked through in this lesson, this condition is no longer met.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"demonstrate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'model-thinking\\': \\'the difficulty is choosing between approaches, not executing one\\', \\'derive\\': \\'the result must be justified from prior statements, not computed\\', \\'practise-guided\\': \\'the learner is attempting the work, not watching it\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Model a complete method\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The result must be shown to FOLLOW from statements the learner already accepts, and each transformation needs a stated justification.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"derive\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'demonstrate\\': \\'the point is the procedure, not its justification\\', \\'model-thinking\\': \\'steps are chosen from alternatives rather than compelled\\', \\'explain-cause\\': \\'the chain is physical rather than logical\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Build a result from prior statements\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"A named, real misconception exists on the card, and a wrong answer can be written that only a learner holding it would confidently choose. One block per misconception the card declares \\\\u2014 a misconception not on the card does not exist.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'check-understanding\\': \\'no specific wrong model is known; the check only detects failure\\', \\'warn\\': \\'the error is a slip or lapse, not a held belief\\', \\'compare\\': \\'both sides are legitimate\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Distinguish a known wrong model from the target model\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Set apart only the single statement learners should retain. Do not create multiple competing key ideas.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"emphasise\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Mark a high-value statement\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Require criteria, evidence, a judgment, and limitations.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"evaluate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Judge a claim, method, or evidence\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner must reason about instances they have not seen, and the difficulty is the idea itself \\\\u2014 not its cause, its flow, its arrangement, or a representation of it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"explain\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'explain-cause\\': \\'the objective asks WHY, and a mechanism links cause to result\\', \\'trace-flow\\': \\'something is followed as it moves or changes through a system\\', \\'show-structure\\': \\'the difficulty is arrangement, containment, or hierarchy\\', \\'interpret\\': \\'a specific representation is on the page and must be read\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Build a coherent mental model\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The objective asks why, or what happens if, and there is a mechanism between cause and result that the learner must be able to state.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"explain-cause\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'explain\\': \\'there is no cause-and-effect chain, only meaning or structure\\', \\'trace-flow\\': \\'the emphasis is on what moves, not on what causes\\', \\'sequence\\': \\'order matters but no causal mechanism does\\', \\'derive\\': \\'the chain is logical rather than physical\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Connect causes, mechanisms, and outcomes\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Explain what a graph, formula, diagram, table, or result means in context.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"interpret\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Translate representation into meaning\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Specify question, variables, observations, and evidence expectations. Avoid pretending a screen simulation is a paper practical.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"investigate\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Structure an inquiry or practical\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Provide a short, accurate cue that does not replace understanding.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"memory-aid\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Support recall with a compact cue\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State why each decision is made, what alternatives were rejected, and what signal triggered the next step.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"model-thinking\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Expose expert decision making\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Identify the important parts of a system or idea and state each part\\'s role.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"name-parts\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Identify constituent elements\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Begin with a concrete phenomenon, dilemma, observation, or question. Do not explain the full idea yet.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"orient\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Open attention and establish a reason to learn\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner can begin the task but will stall without prompts, partial steps, or hints.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"practise-guided\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'practise-independent\\': \\'support would now be a crutch\\', \\'demonstrate\\': \\'the learner is watching rather than attempting\\', \\'apply\\': \\'the point is first unaided use, not scaffolded rehearsal\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Rehearse with structured support\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"The learner has already succeeded with support and must now perform unaided, with enough repetition for fluency.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"practise-independent\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'practise-guided\\': \\'the learner has not yet succeeded with support\\', \\'check-understanding\\': \\'the purpose is measurement, not rehearsal\\', \\'transfer\\': \\'the context is deliberately changed\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Rehearse without scaffolding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Ask learners to explain what changed in their thinking, what remains difficult, or which strategy helped.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"reflect\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Prompt learners to examine their understanding\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Express steps or events in a meaningful order. Include dependencies and stopping conditions where relevant.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"sequence\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Represent an ordered process\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Show levels, containment, arrangement, or relationships that are hard to infer from prose.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"show-structure\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Reveal spatial or hierarchical organization\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"State what the learner should be able to explain, do, compare, or justify.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"state-goal\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Clarify the expected learning outcome\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Restate the minimum complete model, not a list of disconnected facts.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"summarise\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Compress the lesson into essential relationships\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Something identifiable \\\\u2014 matter, energy, information, money, data \\\\u2014 enters, changes, moves, and leaves, and the learner must not lose track of it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"trace-flow\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'sequence\\': \\'the steps are actions taken, not a substance being followed\\', \\'explain-cause\\': \\'the point is why it happens, not where it goes\\', \\'show-structure\\': \\'the arrangement is static and nothing travels through it\\'}\",\\n        \"status\": \"permitted\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Follow matter, energy, information, or value\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"Change surface features enough that learners must recognize the underlying structure.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"id\": \"transfer\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"\",\\n        \"status\": \"excluded\",\\n        \"teaching_role\": \"Use knowledge in a changed context\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"choose_when\": \"A specific error is predictable at this exact point, and naming it before it happens prevents it.\",\\n        \"exclusion_reason\": null,\\n        \"id\": \"warn\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"{\\'diagnose-misconception\\': \\'the error is a held belief that must be surfaced and tested, not a slip to flag\\',